  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "radiocraft:vertical_antenna_base",
      "title": "Vertical Antenna Base",
      "text": "A stone pad with radials and a $(thing)loading coil$(). Stack $(item)antenna poles$() straight up on it (they taper as they go up) and run coax into the base: that is a vertical. Right click the base to move the coil's tap to the band you want."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Poles for each band",
      "text": "$(li)10 m: 3 poles$(li)20 m: 5 poles$(li)40 m: 6 poles (more of the coil)$(li)80 m: 7 poles (most of the coil)$(br2)Right on: SWR 1.3. One pole off: about 2.5, which a tuner can fix. Off the tapped band it does not match.$(br2)It sends low, like any vertical: less reach by line of sight, more by skip. The coil costs a little on 40 m and more on 80 m."
    },
